 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nSeveral limited-time locks are possible.\n\nConvergent Invoicing: Basic Data\ne The invoicing category for finer control of billing and\n\ninvoicing processes\n\ne The selection characteristic in scheduling that is used for\ncontract-account-dependent derivation of rating, billing\nand invoicing dates\n\ne That no invoice is created or processing is blocked as a\nresult of specifying a lock reason for a master data record\n\ne The target currency for posting of amounts in invoicing\n\ne That a key is entered for determining forms at the contract\naccount level\n\nThis key is used in determining an alternative application\n\nform.\nConvergent Invoicing: Periodic Bills                                            When the system generates periodic bills\nConvergent Invoicing: Individual Charges/Discounts                       The individual charges and discounts you calculate for the business\n\npartner\n\nIn addition, industry-specific fields are also available.\n\nLink: Contract Account - Business Partner\n\nUse\n\nAt least one business partner is assigned to each contract account. Depending on the industry sector, assignment of several\nbusiness partners to a contract account is also allowed.\n\nPrerequisites\n\nAdditional business partners can only be assigned to a contract account if the corresponding contract account category allows\nthis.\n\nFeatures\n\nThe master data for a contract account is divided into a part that is the same for all business partners of the contract account\n(that is, independent of the business partner) and a part that is business-partner-specific. The business partner-specific data can\nbe controlled differently for different business partners.\n\nActivities\n\nIn Customizing for Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable under |}Basic Functions \u00bb Contract Accounts \u00bb Contract Account\nRelationships \u00bb Define Contract Account/Business Partner Relationships \u2122, you define contract account relationships.\n",
